{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WSM6MeltingFreezing",
    "description": "Melting and freezing block of the WRF single-moment 6-class microphysics scheme (WSM6; Hong and Lim 2006), transcribed from the first part of the minor loop of mp_wsm6_run in phys/physics_mmm/mp_wsm6.F90 (WRF 4.8, NCAR/MMM-physics), which the kernel applies IN PLACE, layer by layer and in a fixed order, between the sedimentation of the precipitation and the evaluation of the process rates: (1) melting of snow above 0 C by heat conduction and ventilation (psmlt, HL A33, RH83 A25), (2) melting of graupel (pgmlt, HL A23, LFO 47) evaluated at the temperature already lowered by the snow melting, (3) instantaneous melting of all cloud ice above 0 C (pimlt, HL A47), (4) homogeneous freezing of all cloud water colder than -40 C (pihmf, HL A45), (5) heterogeneous Bigg freezing of cloud water (pihtf, HL A44) and (6) probabilistic Bigg freezing of rain to graupel (pgfrz, HL A20, LFO 45), the last four sharing one supercooling and one latent heat of fusion evaluated after the melting. The physics are the melting RATES psmlt_rate, pgmlt_rate (kg/kg/s) and the freezing RATES pihtf_rate, pgfrz_rate; pimlt and pihmf are total conversions with no rate. Because the block is an in-place step, the quantities the kernel actually applies are INCREMENTS (kg/kg) over the sub-step dtcld with per-process limiters (a melting increment may not exceed the frozen mass, a freezing increment the liquid mass) -- exposed as <process>_inc with dtcld as a parameter, time-step artefacts kept apart from the rates (FORTRAN_BUGS.md N3) -- and the component also returns the state after the block (T_out, qc_out, qi_out, qr_out, qs_out, qg_out) so that a consumer can chain it into the rate components and the tests can close the water and energy budgets against the kernel. Inputs are the state at the START of the block: the sub-step's initial temperature T (the kernel's t is untouched before this block), cloud water qc (unchanged by sedimentation), the post-sedimentation rain, snow, graupel and cloud-ice mixing ratios, density rho, pressure p, and the start-of-step cpm and xl (saturation.esm); the size distributions of the post-sedimentation state come from hydrometeor_slopes.esm mounted as subsystem `sd` (the kernel calls slope_wsm6 right after the sedimentation and reuses those slopes here; mstep, the sedimentation sub-step count of older WSM6 versions, is identically 1 in this version). The transport properties and the ventilation factor are evaluated once at the initial temperature, exactly as the kernel does (work2), while the conductivity entering the graupel melting is re-evaluated at the temperature after the snow melting. Constants: wsm6_parameters.esm (`par`), lib/wrf_constants.esm (`wrf`); templates from microphysics_templates.esm and lib/wrf_air_properties.esm. Consumer-supplied inputs are the rewrite-target ops `input_<name>` lowered in the inline tests through a per-test template library generated by tools/fill_tests.py from the instrumented WRF dumps.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["wrf", "microphysics", "wsm6", "melting", "freezing", "column"],
    "references": [
      { "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., and J.-O. J. Lim (2006). The WRF single-moment 6-class microphysics scheme (WSM6). J. Korean Meteor. Soc. 42, 129-151 (appendix A eqs. A20, A23, A33, A44, A45, A47)." },
      { "citation": "Lin, Y.-L., R. D. Farley, and H. D. Orville (1983). Bulk parameterization of the snow field in a cloud model. J. Climate Appl. Meteor. 22, 1065-1092 (eqs. 45, 47)." },
      { "citation": "Rutledge, S. A., and P. V. Hobbs (1983). The mesoscale and microscale structure and organization of clouds and precipitation in midlatitude cyclones. VIII. J. Atmos. Sci. 40, 1185-1206 (eqs. A25, A28)." },
      { "citation": "Bigg, E. K. (1953). The supercooling of water. Proc. Phys. Soc. B 66, 688-694." },
      { "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics mp_wsm6.F90 at commit 550b5b4 (WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm submodule), lines 667-705 (melting) and 777-830 (freezing)." }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "WSM6MeltingFreezing": {
      "expression_template_imports": [ { "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_air_properties.esm" }, { "ref": "./microphysics_templates.esm" } ],
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": { "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm" },
        "par": { "ref": "./wsm6_parameters.esm" },
        "sd": { "ref": "./hydrometeor_slopes.esm" }
      },
      "variables": {
        "qc": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud-water mixing ratio at the start of the sub-step." },
        "p": { "type": "unknown", "units": "Pa", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Pressure." },
        "cpm": { "type": "unknown", "units": "J/(kg*K)", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Moist heat capacity at the start of the sub-step (saturation.esm cpm)." },
        "xl": { "type": "unknown", "units": "J/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Latent heat of vaporization at the start-of-step temperature (saturation.esm xl)." },
        "dtcld": { "type": "parameter", "units": "s", "default": 60.0, "description": "Length of the WSM6 sub-time step over which the increments are applied." },
        "nu": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^2/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Kinematic viscosity of air at the initial temperature (WSM6 viscos)." },
        "Dv": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^2/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Diffusivity of water vapor at the initial temperature (WSM6 diffus)." },
        "ka": { "type": "unknown", "units": "W/(m*K)", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Thermal conductivity of air at the initial temperature (WSM6 xka(t, den) in psmlt)." },
        "f_vent": { "type": "unknown", "units": "s^(1/2)/m", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Ventilation factor at the initial temperature (WSM6 work2, shared by both melting terms)." },
        "coeres_s": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^(141/50)", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Ventilation moment of the snow distribution; units for bvts = 0.41." },
        "coeres_g": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^(29/10)", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Ventilation moment of the graupel distribution; units for bvtg = 0.8." },
        "psmlt_rate": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Melting rate of snow above 0 C (negative), k_a (T0 - T)/(L_f rho) (pi/2) n0s(T)/n0s (precs1 lambda_s^-2 + precs2 f_v coeres_s) (HL A33); zero below 0 C or without snow." },
        "psmlt_inc": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Snow melted over the sub-step, min(max(psmlt_rate dtcld, -qs), 0) (WSM6 psmlt as applied and dumped)." },
        "T_s": { "type": "unknown", "units": "K", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Temperature after the snow melting, T + L_f/cpm psmlt_inc." },
        "nu_s": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^2/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Kinematic viscosity at T_s." },
        "ka_s": { "type": "unknown", "units": "W/(m*K)", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Thermal conductivity at T_s (WSM6 xka(t, den) in pgmlt, with t already updated by psmlt)." },
        "pgmlt_rate": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Melting rate of graupel (negative), k_a(T_s) (T0 - T_s)/(L_f rho) (precg1 lambda_g^-2 + precg2 f_v coeres_g) (HL A23, LFO 47), gated on the INITIAL temperature being above 0 C as in the kernel; zero without graupel." },
        "pgmlt_inc": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Graupel melted over the sub-step, min(max(pgmlt_rate dtcld, -qg), 0) (WSM6 pgmlt as applied and dumped)." },
        "T_m": { "type": "unknown", "units": "K", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Temperature after both melting terms, T_s + L_f/cpm pgmlt_inc; the temperature at which the freezing block evaluates its supercooling." },
        "supcol_f": { "type": "unknown", "units": "K", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Supercooling T0 - T_m of the freezing block (WSM6 supcol, evaluated once per layer)." },
        "xlf_f": { "type": "unknown", "units": "J/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Latent heat of fusion of the freezing block: L_s - L_v(T) below 0 C, the constant xlf0 above (WSM6 xlf)." },
        "pimlt_inc": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud ice melted instantaneously above 0 C: all of it (HL A47; WSM6 pimlt)." },
        "qc_a": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud water after the ice melting, qc + pimlt_inc." },
        "T_a": { "type": "unknown", "units": "K", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Temperature after the ice melting, T_m - xlf_f/cpm pimlt_inc." },
        "pihmf_inc": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud water frozen homogeneously below -40 C: all of it (HL A45; WSM6 pihmf)." },
        "qc_b": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud water after the homogeneous freezing, qc_a - pihmf_inc." },
        "pihtf_rate": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Heterogeneous (Bigg) freezing rate of cloud water, B' (exp(B min(T0 - T_m, 50 K)) - 1) rho qc_b^2/(rho_w N_c) (HL A44); the physics of pihtf." },
        "pihtf_inc": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud water frozen heterogeneously over the sub-step below 0 C, min(pihtf_rate dtcld, qc_b) (WSM6 pfrzdtc)." },
        "pgfrz_rate": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Probabilistic (Bigg) freezing rate of rain to graupel, 20 pi^2 B' n0r rho_w/rho (exp(B min(T0 - T_m, 50 K)) - 1) lambda_r^-7 (HL A20, LFO 45); the physics of pgfrz." },
        "pgfrz_inc": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Rain frozen to graupel over the sub-step below 0 C, min(pgfrz_rate dtcld, qr) (WSM6 pfrzdtr)." },
        "T_out": { "type": "unknown", "units": "K", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Temperature after the block, T_a + xlf_f/cpm (pihmf_inc + pihtf_inc + pgfrz_inc) (the kernel's t at which the process rates are evaluated)." },
        "qc_out": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud water after the block, qc_b - pihtf_inc." },
        "qi_out": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud ice after the block, qi - pimlt_inc + pihmf_inc + pihtf_inc." },
        "qr_out": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Rain after the block, qr - psmlt_inc - pgmlt_inc - pgfrz_inc (the melting increments are negative)." },
        "qs_out": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Snow after the block, qs + psmlt_inc." },
        "qg_out": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Graupel after the block, qg + pgmlt_inc + pgfrz_inc." }
      },
      "equations": [
        { "lhs": "qc", "rhs": { "op": "input_qc", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "p", "rhs": { "op": "input_p", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "cpm", "rhs": { "op": "input_cpm", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "xl", "rhs": { "op": "input_xl", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "nu", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "kinematic_viscosity_of_air", "bindings": { "T": "sd.T", "rho": "sd.rho", "coef": "par.viscos_coef", "T_sutherland": "par.sutherland_T" } } },
        { "lhs": "Dv", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "diffusivity_of_water_vapor", "bindings": { "T": "sd.T", "p": "p", "coef": "par.diffus_coef", "expn": "par.diffus_exp" } } },
        { "lhs": "ka", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "thermal_conductivity_of_air", "bindings": { "nu": "nu", "rho": "sd.rho", "coef": "par.xka_coef" } } },
        { "lhs": "f_vent", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ventilation_factor", "bindings": { "nu": "nu", "Dv": "Dv", "rho": "sd.rho", "rho0": "wrf.rhoair0" } } },
        { "lhs": "coeres_s", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ventilation_slope_factor", "bindings": { "rslope": "sd.rslope_s", "rslopeb": "sd.rslopeb_s", "rslope2": "sd.rslope2_s" } } },
        { "lhs": "coeres_g", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ventilation_slope_factor", "bindings": { "rslope": "sd.rslope_g", "rslopeb": "sd.rslopeb_g", "rslope2": "sd.rslope2_g" } } },
        { "lhs": "psmlt_rate", "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
            { "op": "and", "args": [{ "op": ">", "args": ["sd.T", "wrf.svpt0"] }, { "op": ">", "args": ["sd.qs", 0] }] },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "melting_by_conduction", "bindings": { "ka": "ka", "T": "sd.T", "t0": "wrf.svpt0", "xlf": "wrf.xlf", "rho": "sd.rho", "geom": { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["wrf.piconst", 2] }, "sd.n0sfac"] }, "rslope2": "sd.rslope2_s", "coeres": "coeres_s", "f_vent": "f_vent", "c1": "sd.precs1", "c2": "sd.precs2" } },
            0 ] } },
        { "lhs": "psmlt_inc", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "melting_increment_limiter", "bindings": { "rate": "psmlt_rate", "q": "sd.qs", "dt": "dtcld" } } },
        { "lhs": "T_s", "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": ["sd.T", { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["wrf.xlf", "cpm"] }, "psmlt_inc"] }] } },
        { "lhs": "nu_s", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "kinematic_viscosity_of_air", "bindings": { "T": "T_s", "rho": "sd.rho", "coef": "par.viscos_coef", "T_sutherland": "par.sutherland_T" } } },
        { "lhs": "ka_s", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "thermal_conductivity_of_air", "bindings": { "nu": "nu_s", "rho": "sd.rho", "coef": "par.xka_coef" } } },
        { "lhs": "pgmlt_rate", "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
            { "op": "and", "args": [{ "op": ">", "args": ["sd.T", "wrf.svpt0"] }, { "op": ">", "args": ["sd.qg", 0] }] },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "melting_by_conduction", "bindings": { "ka": "ka_s", "T": "T_s", "t0": "wrf.svpt0", "xlf": "wrf.xlf", "rho": "sd.rho", "geom": 1, "rslope2": "sd.rslope2_g", "coeres": "coeres_g", "f_vent": "f_vent", "c1": "sd.precg1", "c2": "sd.precg2" } },
            0 ] } },
        { "lhs": "pgmlt_inc", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "melting_increment_limiter", "bindings": { "rate": "pgmlt_rate", "q": "sd.qg", "dt": "dtcld" } } },
        { "lhs": "T_m", "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": ["T_s", { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["wrf.xlf", "cpm"] }, "pgmlt_inc"] }] } },
        { "lhs": "supcol_f", "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["wrf.svpt0", "T_m"] } },
        { "lhs": "xlf_f", "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [{ "op": "<", "args": ["supcol_f", 0] }, "wrf.xlf", { "op": "-", "args": ["wrf.xls", "xl"] }] } },
        { "lhs": "pimlt_inc", "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [{ "op": "and", "args": [{ "op": "<", "args": ["supcol_f", 0] }, { "op": ">", "args": ["sd.qi", 0] }] }, "sd.qi", 0] } },
        { "lhs": "qc_a", "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": ["qc", "pimlt_inc"] } },
        { "lhs": "T_a", "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["T_m", { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["xlf_f", "cpm"] }, "pimlt_inc"] }] } },
        { "lhs": "pihmf_inc", "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [{ "op": "and", "args": [{ "op": ">", "args": ["supcol_f", "par.supcol_homog"] }, { "op": ">", "args": ["qc_a", 0] }] }, "qc_a", 0] } },
        { "lhs": "qc_b", "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["qc_a", "pihmf_inc"] } },
        { "lhs": "pihtf_rate", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "biggs_freezing_of_cloud_water", "bindings": { "qc": "qc_b", "rho": "sd.rho", "T": "T_m", "t0": "wrf.svpt0", "rho_w": "wrf.rhowater", "N_c": "par.xncr", "pfrz1": "par.pfrz1", "pfrz2": "par.pfrz2", "supcol_max": "par.supcol_max" } } },
        { "lhs": "pihtf_inc", "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
            { "op": "and", "args": [{ "op": ">", "args": ["supcol_f", 0] }, { "op": ">", "args": ["qc_b", "par.qmin"] }] },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "freezing_increment_limiter", "bindings": { "rate": "pihtf_rate", "q": "qc_b", "dt": "dtcld" } },
            0 ] } },
        { "lhs": "pgfrz_rate", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "biggs_freezing_of_rain", "bindings": { "rslope": "sd.rslope_r", "rslope3": "sd.rslope3_r", "rho": "sd.rho", "T": "T_m", "t0": "wrf.svpt0", "rho_w": "wrf.rhowater", "n0r": "par.n0r", "pfrz1": "par.pfrz1", "pfrz2": "par.pfrz2", "supcol_max": "par.supcol_max", "coef": "par.pgfrz_coef", "pi": "wrf.piconst" } } },
        { "lhs": "pgfrz_inc", "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
            { "op": "and", "args": [{ "op": ">", "args": ["supcol_f", 0] }, { "op": ">", "args": ["sd.qr", 0] }] },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "freezing_increment_limiter", "bindings": { "rate": "pgfrz_rate", "q": "sd.qr", "dt": "dtcld" } },
            0 ] } },
        { "lhs": "T_out", "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": ["T_a", { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["xlf_f", "cpm"] }, { "op": "+", "args": ["pihmf_inc", "pihtf_inc", "pgfrz_inc"] }] }] } },
        { "lhs": "qc_out", "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["qc_b", "pihtf_inc"] } },
        { "lhs": "qi_out", "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["sd.qi", "pimlt_inc"] }, "pihmf_inc", "pihtf_inc"] } },
        { "lhs": "qr_out", "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["sd.qr", { "op": "+", "args": ["psmlt_inc", "pgmlt_inc", "pgfrz_inc"] }] } },
        { "lhs": "qs_out", "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": ["sd.qs", "psmlt_inc"] } },
        { "lhs": "qg_out", "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": ["sd.qg", "pgmlt_inc", "pgfrz_inc"] } }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "qss_step250_row23_col25_melting_and_freezing",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_quarter_ss idealized supercell (GNU real32 build, dx = 2 km, dt = 12 s, 40 layers, WSM6 only) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump with esm_dump_inner hooks inside mp_wsm6_run of the ctessum-claude/MMM-physics fork, commit 52cfbd7) and replayed through the real64 (kind_phys = real64) standalone kernels/wsm6_driver at the WRF step. The block is an in-place step, so the test is an INCREMENT test over the kernel's sub-step dtcld = 12 s (no small-dt replay; the increments are the quantities the kernel applies): the inputs are the state at the start of the block -- the kernel's input temperature t and cloud water qc (untouched before the block), den, p, the start-of-step cpm and xl, and the post-sedimentation rain, snow, graupel and cloud ice, which the kernel does not dump and are reconstructed exactly from what it does dump: qs = qs_rates - psmlt, qg = qg_rates - pgmlt - pgfrz, qr = qr_rates + psmlt + pgmlt + pgfrz, qi = qi_rates + pimlt - pihmf - pihtf, where psmlt and pgmlt are the dumped increments, pimlt = qc_rates - qc (warm layers), pihmf = qc (layers colder than -40 C), pihtf = qc - qc_rates - pihmf (other cold layers) follow from the cloud-water budget and pgfrz from the energy budget (t_rates - T_after_melting_and_cloud_freezing) cpm/(xls - xl) of the real64 replay. The expected values are the dumped psmlt/pgmlt increments, the budget-derived pimlt/pihmf/pihtf/pgfrz increments, and the state after the block (t_rates, qc/qi/qr/qs/qg_rates). Residual esm-vs-real64 mismatch: the kernel's real32 constants and literals (FORTRAN_BUGS.md N2), in particular pfrz2 = 0.6600000262 whose rounding is amplified by the 50 K supercooling cap to 1.3e-6 relative in exp(pfrz2 supcol) and hence in pihtf_rate and pgfrz_rate; and t0c = 273.1499939 K, whose 6e-6 K offset is amplified by the melting rates being proportional to T - T0 = 0.15 K in the only unlimited melting layer (1.6e-5 relative). Measured with zero tolerances: the melting increments agree to 1.6e-5 relative where unlimited (exactly where limited, since then they equal the frozen mass), pihtf to 2.7e-6 relative, pgfrz to 1e-9 absolute (1.4e-6 of column maximum), and the final temperature to 8e-7 K (the pgfrz rounding times L_f/cpm). Tolerances: melting increments Linf 1e-4 of column maximum and rel 5e-5 spot checks at the one layer (8) where the increment is unlimited (rate x dtcld is below the snow/graupel mass), which also pins psmlt_rate and pgmlt_rate = increment/dtcld there; freezing increments Linf 1e-5 of column maximum and rel 1e-5 spot checks at unlimited layers; pimlt/pihmf exact (abs 0); final state Linf 2e-6 K (rel 1e-8 spot checks) and 1e-6 of the column maximum of each species (1e-4 for snow, which inherits the melting tolerance). Regime: supercell step 250 (t = 50 min), row j = 23, column i = 25: layers 1-8 above 0 C with all snow melting out in 2-7 and the snow and graupel melting unlimited in layer 8 (T = 273.3 K); cloud ice melts in the same layers; heterogeneous freezing of cloud water in layers 12-19 (unlimited) and homogeneous freezing above layer 20 (T < -40 C); rain freezes in layers 9-15 (unlimited, up to 1.4e-4 kg/kg) and completely from layer 16 up.",
          "parameter_overrides": {
            "dtcld": 12.0
          },
          "expression_template_imports": [
            {
              "ref": "./tests/qss_step250_row23_col25_melting_and_freezing_inputs.esm"
            }
          ],
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 1.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "psmlt_inc",
              "time": 0.0,
              "reduce": "Linf_error",
              "expected": 0.0,
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "k"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "k": {
